// /app/franchize/server-actions/storage-bikes.ts
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// «Зимнее хранение» — owner-facing wall + tracking server actions (2026-09-27).
//
// The winter-storage contract itself is generated by the flowType="storage"
// checkout (actions-runtime.ts, consolidated doc branch). These actions give
// every move a home afterwards:
//
//   getStorageWallAction        → the «Хранение» wall: staff sees the whole
//                                 season, a logged-in owner sees HIS bikes,
//                                 guests get the offer view (no PII).
//   createStorageBikeAction     → manual add (owner from the Mini App, or
//                                 staff on behalf of a phone caller). NOT
//                                 for rent — these are client machines.
//   updateStorageBikeStatusAction → staff moves: заявка → на хранении →
//                                 возвращён (+ отмена). Every move is
//                                 validated against STORAGE_STATUS_TRANSITIONS,
//                                 logged into storage_bike_events and pushed
//                                 to Telegram (owner + crew) — «notifications
//                                 for every move».
//   addStorageBikeNoteAction    → a note from staff OR the bike's owner.
//
// Identity ladder (mirrors bike-wall.ts / SA-001 lesson — a client-claimed id
// alone grants NOTHING):
//   1. signed Telegram actor cookie (verifyTelegramActorCookieValue),
//   2. raw initData fallback (HMAC vs bot token; claimed actor must match),
//   3. otherwise the caller is a GUEST: read-only offer, zero bike data.
// Staff = crew owner / global admin / ANY active crew member (same as the
// bikes wall). There is deliberately NO password path here — the analytics
// password unlocks money walls, not owner PII in storage.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

